# `Files` — reading and writing

`Path` names it; **`Files`** (static methods) acts on it — where your program meets the disk.

## Whole-file shortcuts — the 90% case

One call opens, transfers, and closes internally:

```java
String text        = Files.readString(path);      // UTF-8
List<String> lines = Files.readAllLines(path);
Files.writeString(path, "hello\n");                // create + truncate
```

Append or refuse-if-exists via `OpenOption`:

```java
Files.writeString(path, line, StandardOpenOption.APPEND);
```

## Large file → stream it, don't slurp it

```java
try (Stream<String> lines = Files.lines(path)) {   // lazy, one line at a time
    long errs = lines.filter(l -> l.contains("ERROR")).count();
}   // holds a file handle — MUST be closed
```

A module-07 pipeline whose source is a file. **Slurp small, stream large.**

## The files themselves

```java
Files.exists(p);   Files.createDirectories(p);   // makes parents
Files.copy(src, dst, REPLACE_EXISTING);   Files.move(src, dst);
Files.delete(p);   // throws if absent (honest errors)
```

Every op throws checked `IOException` — wrap or declare it.
